 in this event the Soviet Union became the fourth nation on that list, as " [:a {:href "/athletes/50713"} "Marina Koshevaya"] " won gold, and led " [:a {:href "/athletes/50701"} "Maryna Yurchenia"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/50737"} "Lyubov Rusanova"] " to the medal stand. Koshevaya was dominant in winning with 2:33.35, over 1½ seconds better than Linke’s world record and nearly three seconds ahead of Yurchenia."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "208"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50713"} "Marina Koshevaya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "2:35.14 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "2:33.35 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "204"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50701"} "Marina Yurchenya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "2:37.92 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:36.08 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "211"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50737"} "Lyubov Rusanova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "2:37.45 (2 h4)"] [:td {} "2:36.22 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "98"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47455"} "Hannelore Anke"]] [:td {} [: